{"text": "W. Harry Fortuna\n(415) 317-3654 | wafortuna@gmail.com\n\nwww.wharryfortuna.com\n\nRECENT EXPERIENCE\n\nRADIOLAB/WNYC Studios, New York September-December 2016\nIntern\nHelped team in all phases of production, pitched stories weekly. Transcribed and logged tape, pulled audio selects for\ninterviews and cut promos.\nINVERSE.COM, New York June-August 2016\nScience and Tech Writer/Intern\nProduced four to five articles a week related to science and technology for this online outlet.\n\nSTARFISH MEDIA GROUP, New York January-May 2016\nProduction Assistant/Intern\nResearched and pitched story ideas. Edited and logged video footage. Interviewed sources at Soledad O'Brien's news and\ndocumentary production company.\n\nEXPERIENCE\n\nCRESCENTCITY LOCATIONS, INC., New Orleans 2014-Present\nFounder/Owner/Operator\nRun a company that helps property owners advertise their holding for use by film companies as a set for film or other\ncompany need related to production.\n\nNOLA EVENT PERMITS, LLC, New Orleans 2014\u2014Present\nCo-Founder/Partner/Head of Corporate Management and Development\nHelp run a company that works with film, TV, and event productions to help navigate city and state offices to obtain\nthe necessary permissions and permits according to their event or production needs.\n\nRISSMAN MEMORY LAB, Los Angeles 2013-2015\nNeuroscience Research Assistant\nAssisted graduate students and professors in rendering and modeling fMRI images, organizing data, and creating visuals\nfor presentation. Quickly gained proficiency with neuroimaging programs like Caret, SPMS5, BrainVoyager and MatLab.\n\nVARIOUS TV/FILM PRODUCTIONS, San Francisco, Los Angeles, New Orleans 2004-2015\nLocation Manager (IMDB)\nLocation Managers for film and television, coordinate all practical arrangements for filming taking place outside\nof a sound stage or studio. Organized the movement and logistics of companies ranging from 25 to 350\npeople. Worked on titles such as The Muppets, Dawn of the Planet of the Apes, and Monk.\n\nEDUCATION\nCUNY Graduate School of Journalism M.A., 2016\nHealth and Science Concentration\nSt. Mary\u2019s College of Maryland B.A., 2002\nSocio-Anthropology with a focus on Colonial Archaeology\nNew York Film Academy 2001\nCertificate in Independent Filmmaking\nSKILLS\n\nSOFTWARE: Adobe Suite, Google Suite, Pro Tools, Audacity, MatLab, HTML, CSS, Word Press\nHARDWARE: Nikon DSLR, Canon DSLR, Darkroom Film Development, MAC, PC and Android",
